_notice() {
	cat <<'EOF'
Firefox holds an add-on of the system directory disabled. Open about:addons
one time and make QtCurve the active theme there. While this add-on is not
active, the writer of the qtcurve package removes its style sheets from the
profile. The QtCurve look then follows your theme choice in Firefox.

The writer of the qtcurve package carries the whole look, and the scroll bars
of web pages, into your Firefox profiles. Turn on "Apply the settings to
Firefox" in the QtCurve settings dialogue, and set
toolkit.legacyUserProfileCustomizations.stylesheets to true in about:config.

A theme switch shows at once. Firefox shows a change of a sheet, and the
removal of a sheet, after a restart.
EOF
}

post_install() {
	_notice
}

post_upgrade() {
	_notice
}

post_remove() {
	cat <<'EOF'
The writer of the qtcurve package writes two style sheets into each Firefox
profile of a user. Run qtcurve-firefox-writer --remove to delete those files.
pacman deletes no file under a home directory.
EOF
}
